# Product Submission

This guide explains how to submit a product to the Codexeron Marketplace.

Every submitted product is reviewed before it becomes publicly available.

---

## Before You Submit

Before submitting your product, make sure that:

- You are the original author or have the legal right to distribute the product.
- Your product is complete and functional.
- All required files are included.
- Documentation is provided.
- The product has been tested.
- The product complies with the Codexeron Marketplace Rules.

Products that do not meet these requirements may be rejected.

---

## Submission Process

The product submission process consists of the following steps:

1. Create a new product.
2. Select the appropriate category.
3. Enter product information.
4. Upload product files.
5. Upload product images.
6. Add documentation.
7. Select a license.
8. Set the product price.
9. Submit for review.

Once submitted, the product enters the review queue.

---

## Required Information

Each product submission should include:

- Product Name
- Short Description
- Full Description
- Category
- Version Number
- Supported PHP Version
- Framework (if applicable)
- Tags
- Demo URL (Optional)
- Documentation
- Changelog

Providing complete information helps speed up the review process.

---

## Required Files

Your submission should include:

- Source Code
- Documentation
- License Information
- Installation Guide
- Update History

Additional files may be requested during the review process.

---

## Product Images

Every product should include high-quality images.

Recommended images include:

- Product Thumbnail
- Screenshots
- Dashboard Preview
- Feature Highlights

Images should accurately represent the product.

---

## Review Queue

After submission, your product enters the review queue.

The review process checks:

- Product quality
- Code quality
- Security
- Documentation
- Functionality
- Compliance with marketplace rules

Products may be approved, returned for revision, or rejected.

---

## Updating a Submission

If your submission is returned for revision:

- Review the feedback carefully.
- Apply the requested changes.
- Upload a new version.
- Resubmit the product.

---

## Common Reasons for Rejection

Products may be rejected for reasons such as:

- Incomplete files
- Poor documentation
- Broken functionality
- Security issues
- Copyright violations
- Misleading product information
- Low-quality code

---

## Best Practices

To improve approval chances:

- Test your product thoroughly.
- Write clear documentation.
- Use clean and maintainable code.
- Keep product information accurate.
- Include useful screenshots.

